WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.425 --> 00:00:04.005
Mind Your Decisions. I'm Presh Talwalkar.

00:00:04.465 --> 00:00:11.455
ABCDE x A = EEEEEE. [Six E's in a row.]

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:15.135
Each letter is a different digit.

00:00:15.195 --> 00:00:18.275
The challenge is to solve for each letter.

00:00:19.215 --> 00:00:22.495
This problem was given to nine-year-old students in Taiwan,

00:00:22.495 --> 00:00:27.035
and it was considered so hard that it made the television news.

00:00:27.445 --> 00:00:31.525
One teacher even took 20 minutes to solve this problem.

00:00:31.845 --> 00:00:33.655
Can you figure it out?

00:00:34.145 --> 00:00:37.155
Pause the video if you'd like to give this problem a try,

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:41.520
And when you're ready, keep watching to learn how to solve this problem.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:57.040
Here is one way to solve the problem.

00:00:57.385 --> 00:01:00.575
First consider the case that A is equal to 1.

00:01:01.105 --> 00:01:07.225
In that case, ABCDE x 1 = ABCDE [the same number].

00:01:07.455 --> 00:01:10.735
This will NOT be equal to a six-digit number.

00:01:10.835 --> 00:01:13.995
Therefore, A cannot be equal to 1.

00:01:14.385 --> 00:01:16.705
We'll eliminate this possibility.

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:21.880
From here, let's consider the multiplication in the units column.

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:28.195
We have E multiplied by A is a number that has a units digit equal to E.

00:01:29.055 --> 00:01:32.175
What numbers could result in this possibility?

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:34.900
We can work through the cases,

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:37.800
or you can consult a multiplication table.

00:01:38.335 --> 00:01:43.935
From here, we can actually see which cases have E multiplied by A...

00:01:43.935 --> 00:01:47.305
resulting in a number that ends in the digit E.

00:01:47.895 --> 00:01:50.185
There are only eight possibilities.

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:52.840
We can further refine these

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:56.100
because each letter represents a different digit.

00:01:56.155 --> 00:01:58.765
Therefore A cannot be equal to E.

00:01:58.765 --> 00:02:01.415
And we'll remove two of the possibilities.

00:02:01.925 --> 00:02:04.855
From here, we have only six possibilities,

00:02:04.855 --> 00:02:07.885
which can be classified into two different cases.

00:02:08.055 --> 00:02:11.095
We either have A is equal to 6,

00:02:11.095 --> 00:02:13.435
or E is equal to 5.

00:02:13.925 --> 00:02:16.625
Let's work out each of these cases.

00:02:17.515 --> 00:02:20.065
First suppose A=6.

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:22.900
Where can we go from here?

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:26.985
We're going to convert this multiplication problem into a division problem.

00:02:27.485 --> 00:02:31.795
Notice that if we have the resulting number divided by A,

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:33.800
we'll get ABCDE.

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:36.300
So let's work out each case.

00:02:36.515 --> 00:02:40.500
Here, suppose E is equal to 2 and A is equal to 6.

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:44.395
We can then work out the following long division problem,

00:02:44.395 --> 00:02:47.415
and we'll see which five-digit number results.

00:02:47.935 --> 00:02:50.845
We get the following number [37,037], and the thing is,

00:02:50.845 --> 00:02:53.055
it's not equal to ABCDE,

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:55.880
because we need each digit to be different.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:58.880
We can then work through the other possibilities

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:00.620
in a similar fashion.

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:03.740
We can see that none of these possibilities will work.

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:08.600
Therefore, none of these cases will result in a solution to this problem.

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:11.100
So we eliminate all of these cases.

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:14.280
We then consider if E is equal to five.

00:03:14.655 --> 00:03:18.665
We can again work out these long division problems.

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:22.700
Eventually we will get one case which COULD work.

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:25.660
And that will lead to our answer.

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:28.520
Here is the case that works.

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:32.040
And therefore, we have ABCDE multiplied by A

00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:34.825
is equal to EEEEEE [the letter E six times].

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:36.980
And the number ABCDE

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:43.660
is A = 7, B = 9, C = 3, D = 6, and E = 5.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:46.400
And THAT'S the answer to this problem!

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:50.380
Thanks for making Mind Your Decisions one of the best channels on YouTube.

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:57.700
See you next episode as we solve the world's problems one video at a time!

